      "author_association": "NONE",
      "body": "The size discrepancy occurs because PyTorch's state_dict() saves both parameters AND buffers, while the 27M figure refers only to learnable parameters.\n\nThe puzzle embedding uses a large lookup table that's stored as buffers rather than parameters. This is evident from the optimizer initialization which explicitly uses model.model.puzzle_emb.buffers(). These buffers are included in the state_dict() when saving checkpoints, significantly increasing the file size beyond just the 27M learnable parameters.\n\nThe 2GB checkpoint size is expected and correct: it contains the 27M model parameters PLUS the complete puzzle embedding lookup table and other necessary states for model restoration.",
      "created_at": "2025-10-21T15:07:59Z",
